@spec sonority_spec  src=tests/specs/sonority_spec.lua  loc=213  cases=8
@exercises sonority (sonority)
@surface   sonority.score, sonority.walk

# Intent
  Pins the box score of design/adaptive-tuning.md § What "in tune" means: the
  5-limit column of § Choosing the target chooses the theory, its identity with
  the Tenney height of the sonority's lcm/gcd, and the two invariances that let
  the model hold no reference pitch.
  
  Pins the walk of § The model too: which strands are current at each onset,
  distinctness by step-class, and the bass as the class a released chord
  leaves behind it.

# Helpers
  @fn near(actual, expected, why)  @ 14-17
      -- The doc's figures are given to 2dp.
  @fn gcd(a, b)  @ 56
  @fn lcm(a, b)  @ 57
  @fn tenneyOfSpan(odd)  @ 61-71
      -- Tenney height of the set's lcm over its gcd, taken as rationals: the integers
      -- the coords reach the same number without ever forming.
  @fn shifted(coordSet, prime, by)  @ 74-82
      -- Every coord of the set moved by `by` on one axis, absent exponents included.
  @fn strand(class, notes)  @ 87-91
      -- A strand as the walk reads it: notes carrying when they are struck and how
      -- low they sit, under the step-class they share. The shortlist is the solve's
      -- business rather than the walk's, so these carry none.
  @fn struck(list)  @ 94-98
      -- Strands of one note each, given as { class, ppq, pitch }.
  @fn classesAt(strands, sonorityAt)  @ 100-104

# Cases
  @case 'the 5-limit column of the theory table'  [pure]  @ 108-113
  @case 'the score is the Tenney height of the sonority's octave-free lcm/gcd'  [pure]  @ 117-124
  @case 'the score is blind to where the sonority sits'  [pure]  @ 128-134
  @case 'a repeated member and an octave doubling cost nothing'  [pure]  @ 138-145
  @case 'a block chord and an arpeggio of it hand back the same set'  [pure]  @ 149-161
  @case 'at n one above the arity consecutive sonorities still overlap'  [pure]  @ 165-179
  @case 'a repeated note and an octave doubling each spend one entry'  [pure]  @ 183-196
  @case 'a later strand of a class replaces the earlier one'  [pure]  @ 200-211

